Tottenham, as a [[Premier League]] team involved in the [[2020–21 UEFA Europa League]], was originally scheduled to start playing in the third round on 22 September 2020. However the match, away to [[Leyton Orient F.C.|Leyton Orient]], was postponed after multiple Orient players tested positive for [[Severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus 2|SARS-CoV-2]].<ref name="LEYTOT"/> On 25 September, it was confirmed that Tottenham had received a bye into the fourth round, due to Orient's inability to fulfil the fixture.<ref name="LEYTOT2"/>

In the fourth round, Tottenham beat [[Chelsea F.C.–Tottenham Hotspur F.C. rivalry|London rivals]] [[Chelsea F.C.|Chelsea]] at the [[Tottenham Hotspur Stadium]], 5–4 on [[Penalty shoot-out (association football)|penalties]], after the 90 minutes of play ended 1–1 with one goal for Tottenham Hotspur from [[Erik Lamela|Érik Lamela]] and one goal for Chelsea from [[Timo Werner]]. During the resulting penalty shoot-out [[Eric Dier]], Lamela, [[Pierre-Emile Højbjerg]], [[Lucas Moura|Lucas]] and [[Harry Kane]] all scored their penalties for Spurs and [[Tammy Abraham]], Chelsea [[Captain (association football)|captain]] [[César Azpilicueta]], [[Jorginho (footballer, born December 1991)|Jorginho]] and [[Emerson Palmieri|Emerson]] all scored their penalties for Chelsea. However, [[Mason Mount]] missed his penalty and as a result Chelsea were eliminated. This match was a face-off between [[List of Tottenham Hotspur F.C. managers|Tottenham Hotspur manager]] [[José Mourinho]] and [[List of Chelsea F.C. managers|Chelsea manager]] [[Frank Lampard]] who played under Mourinho at [[Stamford Bridge (stadium)|Stamford Bridge]].<ref>{{cite web|last=Hafez|first=Shamoon|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/54298219|title=Carabao Cup: Tottenham 1-1 Chelsea (5-4 pens) - Spurs progress on spot-kicks|date=29 September 2020|access-date=6 January 2021|work=BBC Sport|archive-date=29 September 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200929222945/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/54298219|url-status=live}}</ref>

Tottenham visited [[Stoke City F.C.|Stoke City]] at the [[Bet365 Stadium]] in the quarter-finals, they went home with a 3–1 victory with one goal each for Tottenham Hotspur from [[Gareth Bale]], [[Ben Davies (footballer, born 1993)|Ben Davies]] and Kane and one goal for Stoke City from [[Jordan Thompson (footballer, born 1997)|Jordan Thompson]].<ref>{{cite web|last=Johnston|first=Neil|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/55327848|work=BBC Sport|title=Stoke City 1-3 Tottenham Hotspur: Jose Mourinho's side one win from final|date=23 December 2020|access-date=6 January 2021|archive-date=8 January 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210108052618/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/55327848|url-status=live}}</ref>

In the semi-finals, Tottenham met the only non-Premier League side still playing up to this stage, [[Brentford F.C.|Brentford]] of the [[EFL Championship]]. Tottenham reached the final with a 2–0 victory at the Tottenham Hotspur Stadium with a goal each for Tottenham Hotspur from [[Moussa Sissoko]] and [[Son Heung-min]]. The semi-finals were played over one-leg instead over the traditional two-legs in order to reduce fixture congestion.<ref name="TOT-SF">{{cite web|work=BBC Sport|last=McNulty|first=Phil|title=Tottenham Hotspur 2-0 Brentford: Jose Mourinho reaches Carabao Cup final|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/55471359|date=5 January 2021|access-date=6 January 2021|archive-date=5 January 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210105220230/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/55471359|url-status=live}}</ref>

==Media coverage==

The match was televised live by [[Sky Sports]] on their Football and Main Event channels.<ref>{{cite web |title=Carabao Cup final: Man City vs Tottenham preview, team news, stats, kick-off time, live on Sky Sports |url=https://www.skysports.com/football/manchester-city-vs-tottenham-hotspur/preview/440532 |website=Sky Sports |date=25 April 2021 |access-date=25 April 2021 |archive-date=25 April 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210425094015/https://www.skysports.com/football/manchester-city-vs-tottenham-hotspur/preview/440532 |url-status=live }}</ref> Presenter [[Laura Woods (English presenter)|Laura Woods]] was joined by pundits [[Michael Dawson (footballer)|Michael Dawson]], [[Micah Richards]] and [[Jamie Redknapp]], with match commentary by [[Martin Tyler]] and [[Gary Neville]].<ref>{{Cite episode|title=Live EFL Cup Final: Man C v Spurs|series=EFL Cup on Sky Sports|network=Sky|station=Sky Sports Football HD|date=25 April 2021|minutes=30 & 143}}</ref> Free-to-air highlights were shown later in the evening on [[Quest (British TV channel)|Quest]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Carabao Cup on Quest |url=https://www.radiotimes.com/tv-programme/e/nmzf2c/carabao-cup-on-quest--series-3-episode-7/ |website=RadioTimes |access-date=25 April 2021 |archive-date=25 April 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210425095946/https://www.radiotimes.com/tv-programme/e/nmzf2c/carabao-cup-on-quest--series-3-episode-7/ |url-status=live }}</ref> The match was shown in the United States on [[ESPN+]], with coverage available in both English and Spanish.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.espn.com/watch/schedule/_/categoryId/119cfa41-71d4-39bf-a790-6273a52b0259/country/us/redirected/true |title=Schedule - Watch ESPN |website=ESPN.com |date=25 April 2021 |access-date=25 April 2021 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210425162904/https://www.espn.com/watch/schedule/_/categoryId/119cfa41-71d4-39bf-a790-6273a52b0259/country/us/redirected/true |archive-date=25 April 2021 }}</ref>

Radio commentaries were provided by [[BBC Radio]] and [[Talksport]]. [[John Murray (sports broadcaster)|John Murray]] and [[Chris Sutton]] were the BBC commentators;<ref>{{Cite episode|title=EFL Cup Football 2020-21, Manchester City v Tottenham Hotspur|series=5 Live Sport|network=BBC|station=Radio 5 Live|date=25 April 2021|minutes=60}}</ref> the match was broadcast on [[BBC Radio 5 Live|Radio 5 Live]] and the [[BBC World Service|World Service]] and streamed via the [[BBC Sounds]] platform.<ref>{{cite web |title=BBC Radio 5 live - Schedules, Sunday 25 April 2021 |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/schedules/p00fzl7g/2021/04/25 |website=BBC |access-date=25 April 2021 |archive-date=25 April 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210425093703/https://www.bbc.co.uk/schedules/p00fzl7g/2021/04/25 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/schedules/p00fzl9p/2021/04/25?utcoffset=%2B01%3A00 |title=BBC World Service Online - Schedules, Sunday 25 April 2021 |website=BBC |date=25 April 2021 |access-date=25 April 2021 |archive-date=25 April 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210425222620/https://www.bbc.co.uk/schedules/p00fzl9p/2021/04/25?utcoffset=%2B01%3A00 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/m000vkdk |title=5 Live Sport - EFL Cup Football 2020-21 - Manchester City v Tottenham Hotspur |website=BBC |date=25 April 2021 |access-date=25 April 2021 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210426022935/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sounds/play/m000vkdk |archive-date=26 April 2021}}</ref> The Talksport commentary team was made up of [[Sam Matterface]], [[Stuart Pearce]] and [[Ally McCoist]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://talksport.com/football/869316/man-city-v-tottenham-live-stream-commentary-carabao-cup-final-team-news-kick-off-time/ |title=Man City v Tottenham LIVE commentary and latest score |website=Talksport |date=25 April 2021 |access-date=25 April 2021 |archive-date=25 April 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210425143904/https://talksport.com/football/869316/man-city-v-tottenham-live-stream-commentary-carabao-cup-final-team-news-kick-off-time/ |url-status=live }}</ref> Local stations [[BBC Radio London]] and [[BBC Radio Manchester]] also carried their own commentaries.<ref>{{cite web |title=BBC Radio London Sport, 25/04/2021 |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/p09fffn1 |website=BBC |access-date=14 May 2021 |archive-date=25 April 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210425181445/https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/p09fffn1 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=BBC Radio Manchester Sport: Big Match Commentary, League Cup final: Manchester City v Tottenham (25/04/2021) |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/p09djv7p |website=BBC |access-date=14 May 2021 |archive-date=25 April 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210425181552/https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/p09djv7p |url-status=live}}</ref>

